**Real root cause found — same capacity issue as before, just in a different zone this time.** `cn-backend-1t43` is stuck in `CREATING` with the exact same error we hit earlier: `ZONE_RESOURCE_POOL_EXHAUSTED_WITH_DETAILS` — GCP has no `e2-medium` capacity in `me-central2-c` right now. This is not our config's fault; it's Google-side capacity for this zone specifically.

**Good news:** your two existing production instances (`cn-backend-4chz`, `cn-backend-cj1f`) are still `RUNNING` and `HEALTHY` on the old template — **your live service is unaffected**. Only the rollout's new third instance is stuck.

